I call the salon back.
The receptionist answers the phone.
"Hello, my name is Maya," I say.
"Hello Madam," she says.
"My appointment is at eleven o'clock on Saturday morning," I say.
"But I have other work at that time."
"I want another time," I say.
"Okay, Madam," she says.
"What time are you coming?" she asks.
"Is there time at half past two in the afternoon?" I ask.
She checks the time.
"Yes, there is time at half past two in the afternoon," she says.
"Then keep my appointment at half past two on Saturday," I say.
"Okay, your time is now changed," she says.
"See you on Saturday afternoon."
"Thank you," I say.
I hang up the phone.
Now my Saturday morning is free.
I sometimes change my schedule like this.
